1
00:00:00,269 --> 00:00:03,218
Before we launch either agent, look at
the workspace badge.

2
00:00:03,654 --> 00:00:08,091
It says Corporate G C P, and the
terminal is open in that workspace.

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:13,530
That's the operating boundary for this
series. The repository in the demo is a

4
00:00:13,530 --> 00:00:14,880
synthetic order service.

5
00:00:15,276 --> 00:00:20,226
We'll start with a read-only task, so by
the end you can compare exactly what the

6
00:00:20,226 --> 00:00:22,539
agent explored with what changed on
disk.

7
00:00:24,227 --> 00:00:28,174
In the terminal, run P W D, then Git
status and Git rev-parse.

8
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:33,568
The path ends in training-orders. Status
displays the lab branch and no file

9
00:00:33,568 --> 00:00:36,761
entries beneath it, so we have a clean
starting point.

10
00:00:37,174 --> 00:00:39,955
The short commit is twenty-seven E four
A B one.

11
00:00:40,277 --> 00:00:44,870
Copy the commit from your own terminal.
You can use it later to reproduce the

12
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:45,816
same inspection.

13
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:52,176
Now ask each client for its version.
This is much faster than guessing from

14
00:00:52,176 --> 00:00:54,090
the menu or from a video.

15
00:00:54,525 --> 00:00:59,539
Record the two values your workspace
reports. If one command is missing,

16
00:00:59,803 --> 00:01:03,646
you can finish the first inspection with
the other approved client.

17
00:01:04,208 --> 00:01:08,723
Use those version numbers when you look
up configuration, model selection,

18
00:01:09,148 --> 00:01:10,837
or skill discovery later.

19
00:01:12,547 --> 00:01:15,901
Open the existing session's model
selector or status view.

20
00:01:16,603 --> 00:01:19,494
Suppose the client shows a friendly
model label.

21
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:23,839
Record the resolved identifier when the
workspace makes it visible,

22
00:01:24,196 --> 00:01:27,233
since the same label can point to
different versions.

23
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:32,139
Then check the configured provider. The
terminal runs in G C P,

24
00:01:32,746 --> 00:01:36,998
while the configured provider determines
where model requests are processed.

25
00:01:37,412 --> 00:01:39,516
Keep both facts in the session record.

26
00:01:41,125 --> 00:01:43,844
Here is the effective policy for our
example:

27
00:01:44,338 --> 00:01:49,713
reading the training files is allowed,
and edits or unit-test runs ask for

28
00:01:49,713 --> 00:01:50,613
confirmation.

29
00:01:50,958 --> 00:01:53,538
Look up the effective policy for your
own session.

30
00:01:54,102 --> 00:01:56,169
This matters even for a simple prompt.

31
00:01:56,536 --> 00:01:58,886
You can tell an agent to inspect a file,

32
00:01:59,173 --> 00:02:03,340
but a proposed command is still a
separate action that needs to fit the

33
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:04,526
session's permissions.

34
00:02:06,421 --> 00:02:11,043
Ask the agent for two paths and one
concrete case: the quantity validator,

35
00:02:11,216 --> 00:02:13,796
its test file, and the test for zero.

36
00:02:14,245 --> 00:02:15,814
Watch it inspect the checkout.

37
00:02:16,315 --> 00:02:21,103
The example points to the validator in
orders slash quantity dot P Y and to

38
00:02:21,103 --> 00:02:23,323
test rejects zero in the test suite.

39
00:02:23,673 --> 00:02:27,435
Those names give us a simple way to
confirm the answer ourselves.

40
00:02:29,278 --> 00:02:33,651
Open the reported validator and the
test. Check that the test actually

41
00:02:33,651 --> 00:02:37,543
passes zero to the validator and expects
a rejection.

42
00:02:38,104 --> 00:02:40,370
Then run the branch and commit checks
again.

43
00:02:40,736 --> 00:02:44,580
In the demonstration the branch header
is still the only status line,

44
00:02:44,936 --> 00:02:46,554
and the commit is unchanged.

45
00:02:46,966 --> 00:02:49,693
That gives us direct evidence about the
checkout,

46
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:52,040
independent of the agent's summary.

47
00:02:54,005 --> 00:02:58,877
Finish by saving the workspace, commit,
client version, model, provider,

48
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:01,629
and permissions next to the two verified
paths.

49
00:03:02,018 --> 00:03:04,603
That's the minimum useful record for the
next lab.

50
00:03:04,994 --> 00:03:09,277
You can now start a session with a clear
boundary, ask a small question,

51
00:03:09,565 --> 00:03:10,747
and verify the answer.

52
00:03:11,183 --> 00:03:15,442
Next, we'll check how both clients pick
up the same repository convention.
